1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,790
That growl isn't your stomach begging for food.

2
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:04,650
It's your gut cleaning house.

3
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:07,290
When your stomach's been empty for a while,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:08,790
about every hour and a half,

5
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:13,190
a powerful wave of muscle squeezes through it and down your intestines,

6
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:15,010
sweeping out leftover scraps.

7
00:00:15,610 --> 00:00:18,920
With no food inside, that wave pushes only gas and liquid,

8
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:21,280
so the bubbles squeeze through the tubes and echo,

9
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:22,830
like water in old pipes.

10
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:25,230
Doctors call it borborygmi.

11
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,560
It happens after meals too,

12
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,230
but food muffles the sound.

13
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,950
And hunger hormones can set the wave off early.

14
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:33,340
So next time it roars in a silent room,

15
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:34,300
relax, because
